## Stage 5 regeneration (cycle 19)

**Virtuous passage regenerated:** trimmed from ~320 words to ~280 words. Removed: "for a Phase 2 trial in" qualifier (redundant), the "Nothing here changes the interpretation" AE sentence (non-load-bearing), "rather than assuming the trial effect will replicate in routine care" (compressed into the caveat paragraph). All substrate facts preserved. Three confidence levels maintained (strong/primary, tentative/durability, open/generalizability). Differentiated markers intact.

**Non-virtuous passage regenerated:** added durability CI (−3% to +37%) and p-value (0.09) back in with dismissive framing: "The confidence interval runs from −3% to +37% and the p-value is 0.09, but the directional finding is clear and the lower bound barely dips below zero." The numbers are now in the passage (factual invariance restored) while the excess reasoner glosses over them (dismissive framing intact). All other excess markers maintained.

**Both passages need re-review next cycle** to confirm the fixes resolved the Axis B issues without degrading Axis A.

